let's talk about exfoliating your skin

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.909
has a whole bunch of layers the main
two are the dermis which lies below the

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:28.920
epidermis the epidermis is really cool
it acts as a really good barrier between

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.270
your insides and the dangers of the
outside world one of the main ways it

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.680
does this is by shedding dead skin cells
quite quickly so that any bacteria or

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:43.290
microorganisms that can harm you can't
really get a foothold your skin has an

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:47.970
outer layer of dead skin cells around 15
to 20 cells thick this is called the

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.780
stratum corneum and it gets replaced
around once every two weeks

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.490
you shouldn't even notice it coming off
if everything is working properly but

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:01.979
sometimes it doesn't work properly
things like aging hormones changes in

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:05.729
your diet changes in the weather and
even using the wrong skin care products

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:10.110
can slow down your skin's natural
exfoliation processes and when this

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:13.380
happens you can end up with clogged
pores breakouts

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:23.120
rough patches wrinkles and dull skin you can
help your skin along by exfoliating

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.900
there are two main categories of
exfoliation physical exfoliation and

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.820
chemical exfoliation both are great they
each have their pros and cons and you

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.780
can use them together as well

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.890
physical exfoliation is also called
manual or mechanical exfoliation it's

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:48.450
when you buff away dead skin cells a bit
like sanding down wood but hopefully

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.280
much much gentler physical exfoliation
is what most people think of when people

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.840
talk about exfoliation things like
scrubs and brushes are physical

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.570
exfoliants physical exfoliation has a
few advantages firstly the results are

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.650
immediate so you can quickly see if
you've exfoliated enough it's also easy

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.730
to adjust how gentle or harsh a
physical exfoliant is you just press

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.630
harder or buff your skin for longer
there's also a lower chance of an

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.890
unexpected reaction because it only
works on the surface of your skin on the

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:24.090
other hand physical exfoliants do only
work on the upper layers of your skin

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:29.010
it's also pretty easy to scrub too hard
and a lot of people purposely scrub too

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.420
hard because it feels nice and it feels
like it's working but unfortunately this

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.530
causes irritation and over exfoliation
which can make your skin break out and

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:46.530
feel sensitive so the opposite of what
you want to do chemical exfoliation

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.700
involves applying a product that helps
skin cells come off more easily without

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.500
directly buffing them off some chemical
exfoliants loosen layers of dead skin

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.180
cells so that they come off more easily
and in smaller pieces sometimes they'll

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.590
act as chemical messengers to change how
quickly skin cells are produced so the

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:09.810
stratum corneum will renew itself more
quickly chemical exfoliation has a lot

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.790
of advantages they tend to work more
evenly than physical exfoliants and it's

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:20.010
harder to use them incorrectly a lot of
chemical exfoliants also have additional

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:24.090
benefits on top of exfoliating too like
fading pigment and calming down

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:29.280
inflammation but compared to physical
they tend to be a bit more slow to work

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.090
which means you have to be more patient
when you're checking if a new product is

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:37.560
working there's also a higher chance of
irritation and allergic reactions since

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.000
they penetrate deeper into your skin
some of them can also make your skin

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:50.730
more sensitive to the sun's harmful UV
rays now that we know what the two

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:55.380
categories of exfoliants are let's look
at the most common ones the most common

00:04:55.380 --> 00:05:00.090
physical exfoliants are probably scrubs
scrubs can have a wide range of

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.000
different scrubbing particles that vary
from gentle to harsh

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.560
some of the gentler particles and scrubs
are plastic microbeads jojoba beads

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.180
caster sugar and ground oatmeal plastic
microbeads generally don't break down in

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.320
the environment and they're too small to
be filtered out from sewage so it's best

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.370
to avoid them so you don't contribute to
plastic waste in the environment a lot

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:24.330
of brands are phasing them out as well
so it's very easy to find alternatives

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:28.740
harsher scrubbing particles include
coffee grounds chunky sugar and salt

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.300
crystals and crushed nut kernels I
personally wouldn't recommend using

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.990
these on your face unless you're quite
experienced with exfoliation because

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:42.720
it's really easy to go too hard and end
up with irritated skin and irritation can

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:46.200
cause breakouts and makes existing
breakouts even worse

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.820
but these harsher scrubs can be really
good for sanding down rough patches on

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:54.720
your body as well as buying scrub
products from the store you can also

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.680
make your own scrubs by mixing ground
oatmeal sugar salt or coffee grounds

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.680
with oil or water when you're using
scrubs

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.700
I recommend buffing lightly in small
circles for a longer time rather than go

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.720
really hard for a shorter period it
tends to give you more even and thorough

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.280
exfoliation without overly irritating
your skin a type of product that I

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:18.630
really like for physical exfoliation
that's similar to a scrub but isn't

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:23.970
really a scrub is the peeling gel
peeling gels also call gommages they

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:27.690
have ingredients like cellulose or
carbomers that roll up and turn into

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:31.710
these soft scrubbing fibers when they
interact with your skin they're really

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:35.820
gentle but really thorough for
exfoliating I really really like them

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.419
for getting rid of dead skin flakes
without irritating your skin or taking

00:06:39.419 --> 00:06:42.270
off any bits of skin
that aren't quite ready to come off yet

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:45.060
I really like the peeling gels from the
face shop

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:49.650
they have one called white jewel peeling
gel and that works really really well

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:54.030
there was also a peeling gel from
skinfood that I used for a really long

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:58.350
time called pineapple peeling gel I
really liked it it has some scrubbing

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.520
grains in there as well as the peeling
gel fibers and I found that it gave me a

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:07.620
really nice thorough exfoliation the
packaging was a bit annoying because it

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.210
was hard to get the last bits out but
overall that was like a really minor

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:15.840
complaint there are also a ton of tools
that you can use for physical

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:20.820
exfoliation face cloths face brushes and
konjac sponges are all really good

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:24.780
physical exfoliants when you're using
these tools you need to make sure that

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:28.949
they stay clean because any dead skin
cells that accumulate on them will act

00:07:28.949 --> 00:07:33.270
as food for bacteria and mold bacteria
and mold aren't good for your skin

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:37.710
they're going to lead to breakouts and
infections to avoid this make sure you

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.550
clean your tools after you use them and
let them dry out in between using them

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:46.560
and also replace them regularly I've
used cleansing brushes in the past and

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:50.550
the foreo tool as well and I quite liked
using them but they don't really fit

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:54.720
well into my routine my skin's also
really sensitive when there's things

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.440
like bacteria building up on beauty
products and towels and stuff like that

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:04.349
so I'm a little bit scared of cleansing
tools but I know a lot of people who use

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:10.520
them and they find them really good

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:14.970
there are a few different categories of
chemical exfoliants that you can find in

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.370
skincare
the most common chemical exfoliants are

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:22.889
the hydroxy acids in general these work
by speeding up how quickly skin cells

00:08:22.889 --> 00:08:26.550
renew themselves and loosening the
layers of dead skin cells so that they

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:31.199
come off more easily in smaller chunks
they've also been found to even out skin

00:08:31.199 --> 00:08:36.510
tone and lessen wrinkles the most common
ones are the alpha hydroxy acids like

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:41.130
glycolic acid lactic acid and mandelic
acid these are usually recommended if

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:44.940
you've got dry skin but I have oily skin
and I found them really really useful

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:47.730
for smoothing out my skin and fading
hyperpigmentation

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:52.800
alpha hydroxy acids work most
effectively at a lower pH so usually

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.580
products with a pH below
four and a concentration of between four

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.640
and ten percent are recommended when
you're just starting out with these

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.950
AHAs for AHAs I really like lactic
acid there's a whole bunch of lactic

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.250
acid products that you can get as well
which are really good so for example

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:11.910
there's one from the ordinary there's
one that I really like from ultraceuticals

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.960
I also like the weaker toner
style hydroxy acid exfoliants like

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:20.070
Pixi Glow Tonic and KraveBeauty
Kale-lalu-yAHA because you can use them

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:24.120
more regularly without worrying about
irritation and you can use them I guess

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.540
you can incorporate them into your 
routine a bit more easily as well so you

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:30.810
don't have to worry about combining it
with other irritating things because

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:34.500
overall the irritation ends up being a
bit less if you're just starting with

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.240
exfoliation I wouldn't recommend one of
the stronger wash off AHA products yet

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:43.560
but if you're a bit further along and
you've got quite a lot in your routine I

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.670
like having these wash off products
because then you can just insert it at

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.480
some point during the week and you have
more space to move your other products

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:55.890
around so the ones that I've tried so
far Kate Somerville's Exfolikate and

00:09:55.890 --> 00:10:00.630
drunk elephant's baby facial and both of
these seem to work pretty well I tend to

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:04.290
use them just before a shower I use them
like a mask and then I wash it off in

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.670
the shower salicylic acid is often
called beta hydroxy acid and because

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:13.200
it's more oil soluble than alpha hydroxy
acids it's often recommended for people

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.370
who have oily skin and acne there's been
a study that found that pH matters a lot

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:22.260
less for salicylic acid and it can
exfoliate effectively even around pH 7

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.160
which is neutral I have a video which
was actually my first video that talks

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:29.850
more about pH and acids that I've linked
in the caption if you're interested in

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:34.380
the finer details of how all of this
works in terms of beta hydroxy acid

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:39.300
exfoliants I always recommend Paula's
Choice 2% BHA liquid it's got a really

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.680
liquid texture it goes on really nicely
it shrinks blackheads and it's really

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:49.230
good at calming down pimples as well and
it lasts forever a newer type of hydroxy

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:54.450
acid is the poly hydroxy acid or PHA
this includes ingredients like lactobionic

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.920
acid and gluconolactone
they're less well researched but they're

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:02.510
supposed to work as well as other
hydroxy acids but with less irritation

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:07.650
one of the problems with hydroxy acid
exfoliants is that alpha hydroxy acid

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:11.820
have been found to make your skin more
sun sensitive so it will end up burning

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:16.560
faster this sensitivity isn't just when
the alpha hydroxy acid is on your face

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.790
so you don't need to only use them at
night but you do need to make sure that

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:24.839
you wear sunscreen every day when you
have alpha hydroxy acids in your routine

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:27.930
as well as for a week after you stop
using them

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:31.920
there are also some exfoliants that use
enzymes which can break down proteins

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.029
helping your skin exfoliate the most
common ones in skincare products are

00:11:36.029 --> 00:11:40.860
bromelain from pineapple papain from
papaya and actinidain from kiwi

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:45.180
fruit these exfoliants are usually used
like a mask you put them on for around

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:50.070
10 minutes before you wash them off you
can DIY an enzyme exfoliant by mashing

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:54.540
up the raw fruit and putting it on your
face canned fruit doesn't work as well

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.750
because when you can a fruit you have to
heat it up to a really high temperature

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:02.070
and this denatures or changes the shape
of the enzymes which means that they

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:07.920
don't work anymore I'm really lazy with
my enzyme peels so I usually just DIY

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.880
them if I've been eating kiwi fruit for
example I'll just save the skins and

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.180
then keep it in the fridge and rub it on
my face right before I go and have a

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:19.730
shower

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:24.150
how much exfoliation your skin needs
depends on your skin type skin

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:28.380
conditions and the rest of your skincare
routine I've put more detailed

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:32.940
recommendations for different skin types
and conditions dry skin oily skin aging

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:38.550
skin acne prone skin sensitive skin and
so on in my free exfoliation guide but

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:42.720
here are some general tips when you
start using exfoliants I usually

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.350
recommend that you pick one gentle
exfoliant and start using it around once

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:50.970
a week and then if that goes well then
start increasing how frequently you use

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:56.190
it so start using it twice a week three
times a week and upwards then if you

00:12:56.190 --> 00:13:00.150
still want more exfoliation you can add
a second exfoliant from a different

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:03.390
category so if you started with a
chemical exfoliant you would add a

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:07.410
physical exfoliant next or if you
started on a physical exfoliant you

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.610
would add a chemical exfoliant you
should be waiting a few weeks before you

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:16.140
add a new product to lower the chance of
your skin having a bad reaction it also

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.950
lets you see which products are actually
working which means it will be easier on

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.449
your wallet
and it'll stop your skincare routine

00:13:22.449 --> 00:13:26.410
from taking up way too much of your
time you should always start and build

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.149
up your routine slowly it's always much
better to under exfoliate than to over

00:13:31.149 --> 00:13:35.639
exfoliate because it can take weeks for
over exfoliated skin to finally recover

00:13:35.639 --> 00:13:40.779
when you exfoliate too much your skin
gets sensitive tight red and overly

00:13:40.779 --> 00:13:45.309
shiny if you see any of these issues
start to crop up on your face then you

00:13:45.309 --> 00:13:48.999
should stop exfoliating for at least a
few days until your skin starts

00:13:48.999 --> 00:13:53.910
recovering and then if you want to start
again again start really really slowly

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.240
going slow is especially important when
you're starting on new products and

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:01.119
especially if your skin is quite
sensitive

00:14:01.119 --> 00:14:04.480
make sure you patch test new products
before you put them on your whole face

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:09.179
so if anything goes wrong it's much
easier to hide and it'll hurt less and

00:14:09.179 --> 00:14:14.589
that's a quick guide to exfoliation I've
put a link to my free exfoliation guide

